Defines with indentation, trailing spaces and a blank-line run, each
called from one context. A body called from collapse is reindented and
loses its trailing spaces and extra blank lines; one called from
pre-line is reindented but keeps every line break (spec §2, WHATWG
ruling 10: pre-line call sites still allow reindenting); one called from
pre-wrap, an attribute value or a textarea keeps every byte.
-- input.gohtml --
{{define "collapse"}}
a  
		b


	c
{{end}}

{{define "preline"}}
a  
		b


	c
{{end}}

{{define "prewrap"}}
a  
		b


	c
{{end}}

{{define "attr"}}
a  
		b


	c
{{end}}

{{define "area"}}
a  
		b


	c
{{end}}

<div>{{template "collapse" .}}</div>
<div style="white-space:pre-line">{{template "preline" .}}</div>
<div style="white-space:pre-wrap">{{template "prewrap" .}}</div>
<p title="{{template "attr" .}}"></p>
<textarea>{{template "area" .}}</textarea>
